### 4.1 What is checked

| Test | What it proves |
|---|---|
| `TestDifferentialRandomUpdates` | 500 random graphs, up to 400 random insert/delete updates each (≈200 000 updates). After **every** update: invariants, exact comparison with the brute-force set-based dataflow (`bruteIdom`), and exact comparison with a from-scratch rebuild. Certificate validated periodically. |
| `TestAllPairsDominance` | `Dominates(a,b)` matches "remove `a` and test reachability from the root" for all pairs. |
| `TestIrreducible` | A CFG with an irreducible loop; tree matches brute force and subtree queries are correct. |
| `TestIrreducibleNaiveCertificateRejected` | The naive "star" certificate that passes the local edge check is rejected by the verifier. |
| `TestDeletionDisconnects` | Deleting the only in-edges of a subtree makes those nodes unreachable; re-adding edges restores correct dominators. |
| `TestCertificateTamper` | Honest certificate accepted; shallow idom, wrong graph, and wrong root all rejected. |
| `TestBoundedRecomputationCount` | A 200-node chain back-edge update reassigns only the local region. |
| `TestEdgeCases` | Single node, empty graph, invalid root (no panic), self-loop and duplicate edge rejection. |

